                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Zap Zone is an extremely fun game, and brings you back to the days of burning stacks of coins in a local arcade cabinet, playing Pac-Man or Galaga. The mechanic of the blaters being based on time, and not ammo makes the player really think about how they are going to tackle the next hallway they run through, and if they have enough time to reach the next ammo box without being knocked down by the adorable Zugs. Zoey, the protagonist, is a nice nod to Pac-Man, but stays her own, with her quips being a nice touch. I recommend this game for anyone who wants to take a nostalgia trip back to the arcade cabinets of yesterday, or anyone who wants to have fun playing a simple but challenging game.",
